[32m+[m[32m- [ ] **Financial philosophy and configurable allocation plans:** Allocate 10% of total *received* income first to Giving to God. Distribute only the remaining 90% according to the default plan: Essential living expenses 30%, Business reinvestment 30%, Emergency savings 15%, Long-term investments 10%, Learning and skill development 10%, Personal enjoyment 5%. These six percentages are of the remaining 90%, not total income; their effective percentages of total are 27%, 27%, 13.5%, 9%, 9%, and 4.5%, respectively. Default the primary currency to ETB. Settings permit currency, allocation percentages, financial month start date, category/subcategory management, budget preferences, privacy and export preferences. Preserve the default philosophy; changing percentages requires confirmation and a clear effective date, and must not retroactively change prior allocations.[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] **Income records and automatic allocation:** Support multiple income records per month with title, amount, currency (ETB default), source, received date, description, payment method, optional supporting attachment and status Expected, Received or Cancelled. Only Received income is available or allocated; Expected and Cancelled income never count as available money. On receipt, atomically create one allocation: first 10% Giving to God, then divide only the remaining 90% among the six default categories. For 10,000 ETB, the result is 1,000 ETB Giving; 2,700 ETB Essential; 2,700 ETB Business; 1,350 ETB Emergency; 900 ETB Long-term investments; 900 ETB Learning; 450 ETB Enjoyment. Amounts must reconcile exactly to the original income, including small amounts requiring rounding and supported currencies with differing minor-unit precision. Processing an income again or editing it must not create duplicate allocations; preserve allocation history. Support income editing, status changes, multiple currencies and accurate date/currency handling.[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] **Financial category management and subcategories:** Track Giving to God allocated versus actually given, with amount, date, optional recipient/purpose and private notes. Provide Essential living subcategories: rent/housing; food/groceries; transportation/fuel; electricity/water; mobile data/internet; personal hygiene; necessary clothing; basic medical; other. Provide Business reinvestment subcategories: website domain/hosting; software subscriptions; digital tools; marketing/advertising; computer equipment; product development/testing; customer acquisition; freelancers/employees; business supplies; other operating expenses; allow linking expenses to a business or project. Track Emergency Savings allocated, deposited, withdrawn, current balance, target and progress. Track Long-term Investments by investment name/category, amount contributed, contribution date, optional current recorded value and notes; support manually recorded regulated savings products, fixed-term deposits, diversified funds, retirement savings and other suitable opportunities. Finance is for tracking only: do not execute investments or promise returns. Provide Learning and Skill Development subcategories: programming courses; software development books; business/finance books; digital marketing training; communication/negotiation; professional certifications; mentorship; workshops; technical training; where practical, link expenses to existing Learning records. Provide Personal Enjoyment subcategories: coffee/occasional meals out; entertainment; hobbies; social activities; personal shopping; gifts; leisure/relaxation; present this category as balanced budgeting, not eliminating enjoyment.[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] **Transaction ledger and history:** Support income, expenses, transfers between allocations, savings contributions, investment contributions and giving records. Each transaction has title, amount, currency, transaction type, financial category, subcategory, date, payment method, description and optional attachment. Support editing, deleting, searching and filtering while retaining an accurate history. Transfers between categories must not be counted as new income or expense; savings balances must not be mistaken for expenses. Reconcile linked income, giving, savings and investment entries so the same amount is never double-counted.[m
