[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Personal Finance & Stewardship Management — proposed implementation plan[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Repository audit and scope[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe current application is Next.js 14 App Router with protected admin routes, a single-admin session (`getSession().isAdmin`), Drizzle/Postgres, same-origin checks on mutations, an existing `media_assets` table, and an AI/storage provider abstraction. No personal finance tracker or finance transactions/income tables exist. The `life_ai_context_settings.finances` flag is only a consent toggle for Life AI context and will not be reused as a ledger. Add a separate protected Personal Finance area; do not connect to banks, execute investments, infer balances, or seed example transactions.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Financial model and calculation integrity[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Store each amount as an integer count of its ISO currency's minor units (wire values use decimal-safe integer strings where DB precision exceeds JavaScript's safe range); never calculate money with binary floating-point.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Keep currencies separate in all totals, charts, allocation budgets and reports. Default the owner's primary currency to ETB while permitting income/transactions in another validated currency. Validate codes against ICU's supported currency values (with ISO four-decimal fund currencies explicitly added) and use Intl currency fraction-digit metadata rather than assuming every currency has two decimal places.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Preserve the two-stage allocation plan as versioned data: Stage 1 gives 10% of a received income to `GIVING`; Stage 2 distributes only the resulting 90% across the remaining categories at 30/30/15/10/10/5 percent. Persist the plan version and exact per-category minor-unit amounts for every allocation run. Use deterministic largest-remainder rounding with stable tie order so all category allocations plus giving reconcile exactly to the received amount, including tiny amounts.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Only `RECEIVED` income is eligible. Create the income transition, linked income ledger entry, allocation run and category splits in one database transaction with unique idempotency constraints. Expected/cancelled income creates no available balance. Reprocessing is a no-op. Received-income edits/cancellations retain prior allocation snapshots and record an explicit new revision/adjustment rather than duplicating rows or silently overwriting history. Allocation-plan edits require a confirmed effective date and only affect future received income.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Track expense, giving, transfer, savings contribution, investment contribution and income events separately. Transfers and contributions move category/account balances but are not new income or expense. Budgets compare planned category allocations with appropriate actual outflows; savings/investment balances derive from their own contribution/withdrawal ledger. Never combine different currencies into a single amount.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Application architecture[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Add dedicated Drizzle tables and one forward-only migration for finance settings/plan versions, categories/subcategories, income records, versioned allocation runs and splits, transaction ledger, savings goals/contributions, investment records/contributions, and attachment references. Seed only the seven owner-approved default categories and percentages—no personal amounts or sample transactions.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Add a server-side `lib/finance/` domain layer for exact money parsing/formatting, allocation arithmetic, plan validation, monthly-period boundaries, and ledger/balance reducers. API handlers call this layer; the browser never performs authoritative allocation or balance calculations.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Add protected, Zod-validated and same-origin-guarded routes for settings/plans, income CRUD/status, transactions, budgets/category adjustments, goals, investments, reports/export and AI insights. Use database constraints and transactions for idempotency and relationships. Treat adjustment explanations and effective dates as required audit information.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Add `/admin/finance` with Overview, Income, Allocation, Transactions, Budgets, Savings & Investments, Reports and Settings views; use the existing protected admin layout/navigation, responsive controls, cards, and empty/loading/error states. All KPIs/charts come from persisted records and selected currency/month.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Integrate the existing `aiProvider` only for explicitly requested financial analysis using actual records; keep insights labeled as educational suggestions, prohibit invented balances/transactions and investment-return promises, and provide an explicit consent/data-scope setting. Do not expose provider credentials.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use the existing media/storage pathway for optional attachments when configured. Current `storageProvider` is unconfigured in this checkout; absent a configured durable upload path, support secure HTTPS or `/manus-storage/` attachment references and clearly state upload configuration is required instead of claiming uploads work.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Implement monthly, quarterly and annual report views; offer CSV exports from real filtered ledger data and browser print-to-PDF, with no generated financial sample values.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Project structure[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`lib/schema.ts` and `drizzle/0022_personal_finance.sql` own normalized persistent records; `lib/finance/money.ts`, `summary.ts`, `report.ts`, `validation.ts`, `persistence.ts` and `api.ts` own deterministic money, summary, report, validation, transaction and access rules; `app/api/admin/finance/**` exposes guarded finance operations; `app/admin/(protected)/finance/**` provides the eight route views; `components/admin/PersonalFinanceWorkspace.tsx` and `app/admin/finance.css` implement the responsive admin UI; `components/admin/nav.ts` and `public/manus-routes.json` register the feature; focused tests cover allocation/reconciliation, currency precision, request validation, summary/report accounting and historical category visibility. Existing Learning, Life AI, opportunities, and other admin areas remain independent.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Design proposal for confirmation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUse a quiet “stewardship ledger” rather than a generic bank dashboard: editorial header and clear amount hierarchy, simple category allocation bars, a chronological transaction ledger, and restrained status cues. Preserve the existing admin shell/surface tokens and navy/blue/gold as the dominant palette, honoring the later request to keep this visually close to the existing admin. Use the brief's #1B4332, #2D6A4F, #D4A437, #C1693C and #FAF6EC only as restrained stewardship/category/status accents, with contrast-safe light/dark theme tokens. Keep the existing portfolio typography stacks (Newsreader/Bricolage fallbacks) rather than introducing a competing global typeface. Avoid decorative chart overload; use simple charts with transparent labels and no invented data.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Material constraints[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis repository has no configured finance database credentials available for safe live writes and no configured file-upload provider in the current checkout. Implementation can add migrations and automated code/schema tests, but must not run the migration against the shared database or create fake financial records. Attachment references can be supported now; durable upload requires storage configuration. AI finance analysis is unavailable until the existing AI provider is configured, but its route/UI can report that honestly.[m
